RIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_not_found", "compensate_unknown_partial", "safe_retry_with_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 416993, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01YKoBvh1CJeydYn5JUMxbK4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 421183, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 should round to 2.66, but it was rounding to 2.67.\n- **The fix:** On the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GPZa2Cu4jSoWqGkMFn3LiV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01W7Q8RKLdMh3ESonJ2VGRCP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DNfsytgwZzLfZcWqM31H5i", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DkoRiME1fZvrXpJXiUUjry", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019gyxCiGu7QHoJQomJqa5vX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Ey4L6nZEHRs1mYHinRuZz1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TmCisrnk5ZMzWaRsdiVMTS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YKoBvh1CJeydYn5JUMxbK4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (FIN-212)", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. This made `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` fail and broke the nightly build.\n\nChange: switch the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 should round to 2.66, but it was rounding to 2.67.\n- **The fix:** On the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}